<article class="env-lemma" id="09J4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09J4">Lemma <span data-tag="09J4">20.48.7</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ be a ringed space. Let $K, L$ be objects of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. If $K$ has tor-amplitude in $[a, b]$ and $L$ has tor-amplitude in $[c, d]$ then $K \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X}^\mathbf {L} L$ has tor amplitude in $[a + c, b + d]$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: use the spectral sequence for tors. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>